    "caveats": [
      "Verify the 0.005 Pa (0.05 dyn/cm²) shear target against the specific literature you cite for intestinal lumen shear; the registry does not list a Caco-2 shear range, so confirm the physiological anchor before finalizing.",
      "Caco-2 must be fully differentiated (mature 21-day monolayer, TEER >= ~300 Ω·cm²) before perfusion; low shear is intended to preserve tight junctions.",
      "Confirm the syringe pump can deliver 0.5 µL/min accurately (use a low-volume glass syringe and prime the line to avoid pulsation).",
      "Check PDMS oxygen permeability and medium gas equilibration; at this low flow the residence time is ~4 min/pass, so ensure O2 delivery is adequate for the cell load.",
      "Validate the actual wall shear empirically (e.g., bead tracking) since the 6·μQ/wh² formula assumes a wide rectangular channel and Newtonian medium."
